============================================================
01. PURPOSE
============================================================

This document defines how the ZyrionOS frontend is constructed
from reusable components.

Document 03 defines how the product LOOKS.

This document defines how the frontend UI is STRUCTURED,
COMPOSED, INTERACTS and REUSES components.

The objective is:

ONE COMPONENT SYSTEM
+
REUSABLE COMPONENTS
+
PREDICTABLE BEHAVIOUR
+
NO DUPLICATED UI LOGIC
+
NO PAGE-SPECIFIC DESIGN SYSTEMS


============================================================
02. CORE ARCHITECTURAL PRINCIPLE
============================================================

Every frontend interface must be composed from reusable,
well-defined components.

A page should primarily be responsible for:

- Page composition
- Data orchestration
- User flow
- Business-level interaction

A reusable component should be responsible for:

- Presentation
- Component-level interaction
- Component states
- Accessibility
- Consistent behaviour


============================================================
03. COMPONENT HIERARCHY
============================================================

ZyrionOS uses the following hierarchy:

FOUNDATION
    ↓
PRIMITIVES
    ↓
COMPOSITES
    ↓
PATTERNS
    ↓
FEATURE COMPONENTS
    ↓
PAGE COMPOSITION


Example:

Button
    ↓
ActionButton
    ↓
ProjectActionBar
    ↓
WorkspaceHeader
    ↓
WorkspacePage


============================================================
04. COMPONENT LEVELS
============================================================


------------------------------------------------------------
LEVEL 01 — FOUNDATIONS
------------------------------------------------------------

Foundations contain system-wide primitives.

Examples:

- Design tokens
- Typography
- Icons
- Spacing
- Motion
- Breakpoints


These components contain NO business logic.


------------------------------------------------------------
LEVEL 02 — UI PRIMITIVES
------------------------------------------------------------

Small reusable UI elements.

Examples:

- Button
- IconButton
- Input
- Textarea
- Select
- Checkbox
- Radio
- Switch
- Badge
- Avatar
- Tooltip
- Divider
- Spinner
- Skeleton


These must remain highly reusable.


------------------------------------------------------------
LEVEL 03 — COMPOSITES
------------------------------------------------------------

Components made from primitives.

Examples:

- SearchInput
- FormField
- StatusBadge
- UserMenu
- ProjectSelector
- DateSelector
- Pagination
- ConfirmDialog


------------------------------------------------------------
LEVEL 04 — PATTERNS
------------------------------------------------------------

Larger reusable interface patterns.

Examples:

- PageHeader
- DataTable
- EmptyState
- ErrorState
- LoadingState
- SettingsSection
- MetricCard
- ActivityTimeline
- CommandPalette
- ModalLayout


------------------------------------------------------------
LEVEL 05 — FEATURE COMPONENTS
------------------------------------------------------------

Product-specific components.

Examples:

- AIComposer
- AIMessage
- AIActivity
- ProjectCard
- DeploymentCard
- DeploymentTimeline
- FileExplorer
- CodeEditor
- PreviewPanel
- BillingPlanCard


------------------------------------------------------------
LEVEL 06 — PAGE
------------------------------------------------------------

Pages compose all lower layers.

Examples:

DashboardPage
WorkspacePage
SettingsPage
BillingPage
DeploymentsPage


A page must NOT duplicate reusable component behaviour.


