============================================================
06. SINGLE RESPONSIBILITY
============================================================

Every component must have one primary responsibility.

BAD:

WorkspaceButton
that:
- fetches projects
- creates projects
- changes routes
- opens modal
- manages billing
- renders button


GOOD:

Button
+
ProjectCreateAction
+
ProjectCreateModal
+
project service


Components must not become uncontrolled
"everything components."


============================================================
07. REUSABILITY RULE
============================================================

Before creating a new component, check whether
an existing component can satisfy the requirement.

If an existing component can be extended safely:

EXTEND IT.

Do not create:

ButtonPrimary
ButtonMain
ButtonNew
ButtonSpecial
ButtonWorkspace

when one reusable Button system is sufficient.


============================================================
08. DUPLICATION RULE
============================================================

The following must NOT be duplicated across pages:

- Buttons
- Inputs
- Search bars
- Modals
- Toasts
- Status badges
- Page headers
- Tables
- Loading states
- Error states
- Empty states
- Navigation controls
- AI composer
- Project cards


If the same UI pattern appears twice,
it must be evaluated for extraction into a reusable component.


============================================================
09. COMPONENT API PRINCIPLE
============================================================

Component APIs must be:

- Predictable
- Minimal
- Semantic
- Extensible
- Type-safe where applicable


Avoid excessive props.

BAD:

<Component
  red={true}
  large={true}
  rounded={true}
  special={true}
  workspace={true}
/>


GOOD:

<Button
  variant="primary"
  size="lg"
/>


============================================================
10. VARIANT SYSTEM
============================================================

Reusable components should use controlled variants.

Example:

Button:

variant:
- primary
- secondary
- ghost
- danger

size:
- sm
- md
- lg


Badge:

variant:
- success
- warning
- danger
- info
- neutral


Components must use the global design tokens
defined in Document 03.


============================================================
11. COMPONENT STATES
============================================================

Every interactive component must explicitly define
its supported states.

Minimum:

Default
Hover
Focus
Pressed
Disabled
Loading
Error
Success where applicable


A component must not depend on accidental browser behaviour
for important states.


============================================================
12. BUTTON INTERACTION CONTRACT
============================================================

Every button must:

- Clearly communicate its action
- Provide visual feedback
- Support keyboard interaction
- Support disabled state
- Support loading state where asynchronous
- Prevent accidental repeated execution when appropriate


Async action example:

Default:

Deploy

Loading:

Deploying...


The component must prevent duplicate submissions
when the operation is already running.


============================================================
13. FORM COMPONENT CONTRACT
============================================================

Every form field should support:

Label
Input
Helper text
Error message
Disabled state
Required indication where applicable


Validation should be understandable.

BAD:

Invalid input.


GOOD:

Project name must contain at least 3 characters.


============================================================
14. MODAL CONTRACT
============================================================

Every modal must define:

- Title
- Content
- Primary action
- Secondary action where necessary
- Close behaviour
- Escape behaviour
- Focus handling
- Loading state
- Error state


Destructive actions must clearly communicate consequences.


============================================================
15. DRAWER CONTRACT
============================================================

Drawers are contextual interfaces.

They should be used when the user needs additional information
without losing the current page context.

Examples:

Deployment details
Project details
AI execution details
Activity details


Drawer must support:

Open
Close
Loading
Error
Content
Responsive behaviour


============================================================
16. TOAST CONTRACT
============================================================

Toasts communicate short-lived system feedback.

Supported types:

Success
Error
Warning
Info


Toast must contain:

Title or message
Optional supporting text
Optional action


Toast must NOT contain:

Large forms
Long explanations
Critical information that disappears too quickly


============================================================
17. LOADING ARCHITECTURE
============================================================

Loading must be contextual.

Use:

Skeleton
when page structure is known.

Spinner
for small localized actions.

Progress
for measurable operations.

Status activity
for long-running AI/deployment operations.


Do not replace the entire application
with a spinner for a small request.


============================================================
18. ERROR ARCHITECTURE
============================================================

Errors have three levels.


LEVEL 01 — FIELD ERROR

Example:

Invalid email address.


LEVEL 02 — COMPONENT ERROR

Example:

Unable to load project information.

[Retry]


LEVEL 03 — PAGE / SYSTEM ERROR

Example:

This workspace could not be loaded.

[Try Again]

[Return to Dashboard]


Errors must provide a recovery path whenever possible.


============================================================
19. EMPTY STATE ARCHITECTURE
============================================================

Every data-driven component must define
what happens when there is no data.

Example:

Project list:

No projects yet.

Create your first project to begin building.

[Create Project]


Empty states must be intentional,
not accidental blank areas.


============================================================
20. DATA TABLE CONTRACT
============================================================

Reusable tables must support where applicable:

- Loading
- Empty
- Error
- Row hover
- Row selection
- Pagination
- Sorting
- Filtering
- Responsive behaviour


Table components must not contain
page-specific business logic.


============================================================
21. SEARCH COMPONENT
============================================================

Search must be reusable across the product.

It should support:

- Query
- Clear
- Loading
- Keyboard shortcut
- Focus state
- Empty results
- Error state


Global search may additionally support:

Projects
Deployments
Settings
Commands
AI actions


============================================================
22. COMMAND PALETTE
============================================================

ZyrionOS may provide a global command interface.

Example:

Ctrl / Cmd + K


Possible commands:

Create project
Open workspace
Open settings
Open billing
Search projects
View deployments
Open AI
Sign out


Command palette must use the global design system.


============================================================
23. NAVIGATION COMPONENTS
============================================================

Navigation must be reusable.

Components may include:

Sidebar
SidebarItem
Topbar
Breadcrumbs
Tabs
SubNavigation
MobileNavigation


Navigation components must understand:

Active
Inactive
Hover
Disabled
Collapsed
Mobile


============================================================
24. PAGE HEADER COMPONENT
============================================================

Standard enterprise pages should use:

PageHeader

Structure:

Eyebrow
Title
Description
Actions


Example:

PROJECTS

Projects

Manage and build your applications.

[Create Project]


This creates consistency across major modules.


============================================================
25. METRIC CARD COMPONENT
============================================================

MetricCard should support:

Label
Value
Trend
Description
Icon
Status
Optional action


Example:

TOTAL PROJECTS

24

+12%

This month


Metric cards must remain compact
and information-focused.


============================================================
26. PROJECT COMPONENT SYSTEM
============================================================

Project-related reusable components:

ProjectCard
ProjectList
ProjectSelector
ProjectStatus
ProjectActions
ProjectHeader
ProjectMetadata


Responsibilities must remain separated.


ProjectCard should NOT become responsible
for deployment execution.


Deployment logic belongs to deployment services
and deployment feature components.


============================================================
27. WORKSPACE COMPONENT SYSTEM
============================================================

Workspace should be composed from reusable sections.

Recommended:

WorkspaceShell

WorkspaceHeader

ProjectRail

BuildToolbar

AIBuildPanel

FileExplorer

CodeEditor

PreviewPanel

InspectorPanel

CommandBar

DeploymentControl


Each component owns its own presentation
and local interaction.


============================================================
28. AI COMPONENT SYSTEM
============================================================

AI is a core ZyrionOS product surface.

Reusable AI components:

AIComposer
AIMessage
AIResponse
AIActivity
AIToolCall
AIStatus
AIProgress
AICodeBlock
AIFilePreview
AIAction
AIError


AI components must be designed
for future agent capabilities.


============================================================
29. AI COMPOSER
============================================================

AIComposer should support:

- Text prompt
- Submit
- Stop generation
- Loading
- Attachment capability where supported
- Context
- Model information where applicable
- Error state
- Keyboard interaction


The composer must remain reusable
between:

AI Chat
Workspace Builder
Agent interfaces


============================================================
30. AI ACTIVITY
============================================================

AIActivity represents an operation being executed.

Example:

ANALYZING REQUEST

Completed


GENERATING PROJECT

Running


VALIDATING FILES

Queued


This component should support
multiple statuses.


============================================================
31. PROJECT FILE SYSTEM
============================================================

FileExplorer must support:

- Files
- Folders
- Selected file
- Expanded folders
- Loading
- Empty state
- Error state


FileExplorer must not directly own backend API calls
unless architecture explicitly requires it.

Prefer:

Service
→
Page/Feature
→
Component


============================================================
32. CODE EDITOR
============================================================

CodeEditor must support:

- File content
- Read-only mode
- Editable mode where enabled
- Syntax highlighting
- Loading
- Empty file
- Error state


Editor technology may change internally.

The external component API must remain stable.


============================================================
33. PREVIEW COMPONENT
============================================================

PreviewPanel must support:

No preview
Loading
Preview available
Preview error
Live project
Refresh


It must not assume a specific deployment provider.


============================================================
34. DEPLOYMENT COMPONENT SYSTEM
============================================================

Reusable deployment components:

DeploymentStatus
DeploymentProgress
DeploymentTimeline
DeploymentLogs
DeploymentHistory
DeploymentActions
