============================================================
36. SETTINGS COMPONENT SYSTEM
============================================================

Reusable settings components:

SettingsLayout
SettingsNavigation
SettingsSection
SettingsRow
SettingsField
DangerZone
SecuritySection


Settings must use consistent patterns.


============================================================
37. RESPONSIVE COMPONENT BEHAVIOUR
============================================================

Components must adapt to viewport size.

A component must not rely solely on page-level CSS
to remain usable on mobile.


Example:

Sidebar:

Desktop:
Persistent

Tablet:
Collapsible

Mobile:
Drawer


============================================================
38. ACCESSIBILITY CONTRACT
============================================================

Reusable components must be accessible by default.

Requirements include:

- Keyboard navigation
- Visible focus
- Semantic HTML
- Labels
- Appropriate ARIA only when needed
- Screen-reader meaningful states
- Accessible contrast


Accessibility must be built into the component,
not repeatedly fixed on individual pages.


============================================================
39. COMPONENT COMPOSITION
============================================================

Prefer composition over giant configurable components.

BAD:

UniversalDashboardComponent
with dozens of props.


GOOD:

Dashboard
+
PageHeader
+
MetricGrid
+
MetricCard
+
ActivityList


Composition keeps the system maintainable.


============================================================
40. BUSINESS LOGIC BOUNDARY
============================================================

UI components should not randomly call backend APIs.

Preferred flow:

USER ACTION
    ↓
PAGE / FEATURE
    ↓
SERVICE
    ↓
BACKEND
    ↓
NORMALIZED RESPONSE
    ↓
STATE
    ↓
COMPONENT


Components display and interact with state.


============================================================
41. SERVICE BOUNDARY
============================================================

Backend communication belongs in:

services/


Examples:

workspaceService
aiService
authService
billingService
deploymentService
projectService


Do not place raw API calls throughout JSX components.


============================================================
42. STATE OWNERSHIP
============================================================

State must live at the lowest level
that genuinely needs it.

Local UI state:

Component


Feature state:

Feature/page


Global state:

Only when multiple unrelated areas require it.


Do not make every piece of state global.


============================================================
43. SERVER DATA VS UI STATE
============================================================

Server data:

Projects
Users
Deployments
Invoices
AI responses


UI state:

Modal open
Selected tab
Expanded folder
Input value
Dropdown open


These should not be mixed unnecessarily.


============================================================
44. EVENT HANDLING
============================================================

Events must have semantic names.

Preferred:

handleCreateProject
handleDeployProject
handleSelectProject
handleOpenSettings


Avoid vague names:

doThing
run
click
action


============================================================
45. ASYNC ACTION CONTRACT
============================================================

Every asynchronous feature must define:

Idle
Loading
Success
Error


Example:

Deployment:

Idle
↓
Deploying
↓
Live

OR

Idle
↓
Deploying
↓
Failed


The UI must reflect actual state.


============================================================
46. OPTIMISTIC UI
============================================================

Optimistic updates may be used only
when the operation is safe and reversible.

For critical operations such as:

Deployment
Payment
Account deletion
Security changes

prefer confirmed backend state.


============================================================
47. DATA NORMALIZATION
============================================================

Frontend components should receive predictable data.

If backend responses vary:

Backend response
↓
Service normalization
↓
Predictable frontend model
↓
Component


Components should not contain dozens
of backend response-format checks.


============================================================
48. COMPONENT NAMING
============================================================

Names must describe responsibility.

GOOD:

ProjectCard
DeploymentStatus
AIComposer
SettingsSection


BAD:

Box1
CardNew
Thing
Panel2
MagicComponent


============================================================
49. FILE NAMING
============================================================

Use consistent naming.

Component:

ComponentName.jsx


Style:

ComponentName.module.css


Service:

serviceName.js


Hook:

useFeatureName.js


Utility:

utilityName.js


Exact naming must remain consistent
with the existing repository conventions.


============================================================
50. CSS ARCHITECTURE
============================================================

Component-specific styles should remain
with their component.

Global styles should contain:

- Reset
- Base typography
- Global tokens
- Global utilities
- Global accessibility rules


Do not create giant page CSS files
containing unrelated component styles.


============================================================
51. DESIGN TOKEN USAGE
============================================================

All components MUST consume
Document 03 design tokens.

Never introduce arbitrary:

Colors
Spacing
Radius
Shadows
Transitions


without a justified system-level reason.


============================================================
52. COMPONENT EXTENSION RULE
============================================================

If a component needs a new capability:

FIRST:
Determine whether the capability belongs
in the existing component.

SECOND:
Add a controlled variant or optional feature.

THIRD:
Only create a new component
if the responsibility is genuinely different.


============================================================
53. DEPRECATION RULE
============================================================

Old components must not be silently abandoned.

When replacing a component:

1. Identify consumers.
2. Migrate consumers.
3. Verify behaviour.
4. Remove obsolete component.
5. Update documentation.


No dead UI architecture should remain unnecessarily.


============================================================
54. TESTABILITY
============================================================

Important reusable components must be testable.

Priority components:

- Authentication forms
- AI composer
- Project creation
- Deployment controls
- Billing actions
- Navigation
- Modals
- Forms
- Data tables


Tests should focus on behaviour,
not implementation details.


============================================================
55. PERFORMANCE
============================================================

Components must avoid unnecessary rendering.

Important areas:

- AI streaming
- Code editor
- Large project lists
- Deployment logs
- Tables
- Chat history


Use appropriate:

Memoization
Virtualization
Pagination
Lazy loading


Only when justified by actual requirements.


============================================================
56. SECURITY
============================================================

Frontend components must never assume
that UI visibility equals authorization.

Example:

Hiding:

Delete Project

does NOT provide security.


Authorization must be enforced by backend.


Frontend may reflect permissions,
but backend remains authoritative.


============================================================
57. COMPONENT SECURITY RULE
============================================================

Never expose:

- Secrets
- Private API keys
- Internal credentials
- Sensitive backend configuration


through reusable UI components.


============================================================
58. UX CONSISTENCY RULE
============================================================

The same interaction must behave consistently.

Example:

If Enter submits one AI composer,
the same composer component must behave
the same way wherever reused.


If Escape closes one modal,
all standard modals should follow the same contract.


============================================================
59. NO MAGIC BEHAVIOUR
============================================================

Components must not contain unexplained behaviour.

Every significant interaction should have
a clear reason and ownership.


Avoid:

Hidden timers
Random redirects
Unexpected navigation
Silent state resets
Unexpected data mutations


============================================================
60. PAGE COMPOSITION RULE
============================================================

Pages should be readable at a glance.

A page file should conceptually look like:

Page
    |
    +-- Layout
    +-- Header
    +-- Main Sections
    +-- Components
    +-- Feature Actions


It should NOT become:

Page
    |
    +-- 2000 lines of duplicated UI
    +-- repeated styles
    +-- raw API calls
    +-- business logic
    +-- random state


============================================================
61. FULL-PAGE MODULE RULE
============================================================

Major navigation actions must transition
to their complete page/module.

Examples:

Create Project
→ Workspace

Settings
→ Settings Page

Billing
→ Billing Page

Deployments
→ Deployment Page

Projects
→ Projects Page


Do not implement a major module
as a tiny nested card unless it is explicitly
defined as a modal/contextual interaction.


============================================================
62. GLOBAL INTERACTION CONTRACT
============================================================

Users should learn ZyrionOS once.

Therefore:

Buttons behave consistently.
Forms behave consistently.
Navigation behaves consistently.
Modals behave consistently.
Search behaves consistently.
AI interactions behave consistently.
Loading behaves consistently.
Errors behave consistently.


