============================================================

Before approving a reusable component:

[ ] Single responsibility
[ ] Reusable
[ ] Accessible
[ ] Responsive
[ ] Uses design tokens
[ ] Defines states
[ ] Handles loading where required
[ ] Handles error where required
[ ] Does not duplicate existing component
[ ] Does not contain unnecessary backend logic
[ ] Has semantic naming
[ ] Has predictable props
[ ] Does not introduce random styling


============================================================
64. PAGE REVIEW CHECKLIST
============================================================

Before approving a page:

[ ] Uses global layout
[ ] Uses reusable components
[ ] Uses Document 03 visual system
[ ] Uses correct page hierarchy
[ ] Uses full available space where appropriate
[ ] Handles loading
[ ] Handles error
[ ] Handles empty state
[ ] Handles responsive layout
[ ] Handles keyboard interaction
[ ] Contains no unnecessary duplicated UI
[ ] Contains no random visual rules


============================================================
65. FINAL ARCHITECTURAL CONTRACT
============================================================

ZyrionOS frontend must be built as a SYSTEM,
not as a collection of pages.

The architecture is:

DESIGN TOKENS
    ↓
UI PRIMITIVES
    ↓
COMPOSITES
    ↓
PATTERNS
    ↓
FEATURE COMPONENTS
    ↓
PAGES
    ↓
APPLICATION


Backend communication:

COMPONENT
    ↓
FEATURE / PAGE
    ↓
SERVICE
    ↓
API
    ↓
BACKEND


This separation must remain clear.


============================================================
66. NON-NEGOTIABLE RULES
============================================================

RULE 01:

Do not duplicate reusable components.


RULE 02:

Do not create page-specific versions
of global components without a real architectural reason.


RULE 03:

Do not place raw backend API calls randomly
inside presentation components.


RULE 04:

Do not invent colors or visual tokens.


RULE 05:

Do not create giant components
with unrelated responsibilities.


RULE 06:

Do not make global state unnecessarily.


RULE 07:

Do not treat frontend visibility
as backend authorization.


RULE 08:

Do not sacrifice responsive behaviour
for desktop-only appearance.


RULE 09:

Do not silently change established component behaviour.


RULE 10:

Do not bypass this architecture
for temporary shortcuts.


============================================================
67. FINAL STANDARD
============================================================

The objective is not simply:

"Make the page look good."

The objective is:

"Build a frontend system in which every page
automatically feels like ZyrionOS."


A new page should inherit:

- Brand
- Typography
- Components
- Interactions
- States
- Accessibility
- Responsiveness
- Enterprise behaviour


without rebuilding the system from zero.


